# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): `REQ-ASK` in a joint model with a scenario (L §6.1, §6.4), the reality of
# L6_4_joint_scenario. The request names x (the scenario's ask), then a.zz, which the member a doesn't declare: the
# run prints the one refusal and x isn't answered. Was a crash: `member_ask` raised its `LOAD-NAME` outside any catch
# (`TallyError: LOAD-NAME no ask a.zz`).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "26a08dc22b514dc0b6eb7c1263103f06b216244b4ed980752bbc810412d05e45"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "a8bf3b260e60f625766da425a660f922557f525c28dcf8ed70567ec64d600ccc"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index jy = year 2025..2027

def income_sum[y in jy]: num PLN = a.income[y] + b.income at reader

ask j1: income_sum[y] for y in jy law 2026-12-31
ask j2: a.tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
ask j3: a.rate law 2026-12-31
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2025..2027
input income[y in yrs]: money PLN
input rate: num
def tax[y in yrs]: num PLN = income[y] * rate at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income[2025] = 100 000.00 PLN
  income[2026] = 120 000.00 PLN
  income[2027] = 130 000.00 PLN
  rate = 0.12

ask q: tax[2026] law 2026-12-31
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input income: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2025..
  known 2025-01-01
  income = 80 000.00 PLN

ask q: income law 2026-12-31
=== sx.tally
scenario sx over family
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

source t "plan"

version up
  cite t
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-10-15
  replace a.rate = 0.2

ask x: a.tax[2026] in sx law 2026-12-31
ask x0: a.tax[2026] in family law 2026-12-31
=== expect x a.zz
refused: REQ-ASK no ask a.zz
